w it's a it's been a long time in a  long time and it would be an  extraordinary thing to do and there  would be obviously blowback from frankly  the Trump base which is still on the  side of Roy Moore the the nativist wing  of the party which continues to support  him so it's a it's a tricky proposition  there's no easy situation here and by  the way if they lose this seat  they're already slim margin in the  Senate of two votes is cut in half  yeah imperil imperils everything else  that they're trying to do meanwhile  Democratic Democrats have their own  dilemma here with the sexual harassment  allegations against Al Franken he's  owned up to these there's gonna be an  ethics hearing is how damaging is this  to Franken and wood and what are the  Democrats to do about this it's very  damaging and his initial response was  was a little casual and and and you know  dismissive about this but he eventually  put out a statement apologizing and  taking responsibility promising to  cooperate with the ethics investigation  in the Senate we are at a real  inflection point I think in this country  when it comes to issues of sexual  harassment and assault we have seen a  men at the highest levels of news and  entertainment and politics accused of  sexual misconduct going back decades and  decades and I think whether it was the  election of President Trump who had his  own accusers coming forward or something  else that precipitated it  there are just a lot of women coming  forward and saying enough is enough to  see change it's not Hilda Kapur thanks  very much for being with us this morning  thank you
 

